From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 22:13:05 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Chunk unload margin: look only at the strip a move uncovers,
 make no empty instances

The margin's move looked up every chunk of the new view square (289 hash lookups and list scans a
crossing) where only the strip outside the old view square can be new; and filterChunkLoadQueue,
widened to the margin, called getPlayerInstance(create) on every chunk of its spiral, leaving an
empty PlayerChunk in every margin chunk for good. On the VPS SG bench movePlayer +
filterChunkLoadQueue had become 8% of the process. The spiral now creates nothing and returns at
once when nothing is queued, view-distance growth is centred on the managed position the
invariant uses, and the index audit checks the view squares (in view watched, nothing past the
margin, no instance without a player).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

